# After `$findsNoMember(object, "missing")` returns true, the library's source may omit a read: `object.missing` is undefined and costs nothing.
# The true result rests on the shape, on bits of the cell and on the class's guard for that name, which the runtime invalidates.
# With testing=CheckWalkAtRunTime the true result is checked against the object itself, by a VM inquiry that reads no guard. 2305 means "nothing, answered by the proof that a lookup finds nothing".
